- there may be an overlap between a proton from the SD process on one side and a beam halo proton on the opposite side, and an activity in the central detector from diffractive state; it is supressed by the rapidity gap vetos and rather low beam halo rate; * two beam halo protons on opposite sides + an inelastic interaction.

The above backgrounds are further discussed in the following sections.

