The last step involved proper normalisation of the \(\chi^{2}_{dE/dx}\) and \(m_{\rm TOF}^{2}\) histograms. Predictions for each true-level pair type were normalised independently, but the same normalisation was preserved for all quantities and for all reconstructed pair types. Normalisation factors \(F_{X}^{\rm MC}\) of the \(\chi^{2}_{dE/dx}\) and \(m_{\rm TOF}^{2}\) histograms representing prediction for exclusive \(XX\) was established such that the number of predicted \(XX\) events in the \(XX\) signal-dominating region (fiducial region of \(\chi^{2}_{dE/dx}(XX)<6\)), \(N_{X\to X,\rm fid}^{\rm MC}\), was equal to the number of measured \(XX\) events in that region (\(N_{X,\rm fid}^{\rm data}\)) less a number of non-exclusive background events in the same region (\(N_{X,\rm fid}^{\rm non-excl}\)) extracted with a method introduced in Sec. 10.2.1. It is expressed with the formula:

