#### TPC track quality cuts variation

Sensitivity of the measured fiducial cross sections on the variation of the quality cuts used in the TPC tracks selection, was also tested. Any change of these cuts required re-calculation of the TPC track reconstruction and TOF matching efficiencies (the latter is conditional w.r.t. the former). Two types of working points were evaluated, "loose" and "tight", with different sets of cuts on \(d_{0}\), \(N_{\rm fit}^{\rm hits}\) and \(N_{\rm dE/dx}^{\rm hits}\) (cuts SC3.4) compared to the nominal working point. The loose and tight cuts are defined as follows:

* loose cuts on the numbers of hit points: \(N_{\rm hits}^{\rm fit}\geq 20\), \(N_{\rm hits}^{\rm dE/dx}\geq 12\),
* tight cuts on the numbers of hit points: \(N_{\rm hits}^{\rm fit}\geq 28\), \(N_{\rm hits}^{\rm dE/dx}\geq 17\),
* loose \(d_{0}\) cut: \(|d_{0}|<3\) cm,
* tight \(d_{0}\) cut: \(|d_{0}|<1\) cm.

Observed ratios of the cross-sections obtained with modified cuts and accordingly redefined TPC and TOF efficiencies, to the nominal cross-section, are shown in Fig. 12.17 as a function of the \(\pi^{+}\pi^{-}\) pair invariant mass. The upward and downward relative changes of the cross-sections were added in quadrature. The resulting systematic uncertainty of the cross-section related to the TPC track quality cuts was estimated to be \(\pm 1.5\%\).

