The efficiency is plotted as a function of the higher and lower \(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) of two tracks in Fig. 18.5b. It is evident from the plot that restriction of the fiducial region to \(\max(p_{\mathrm{T}})>0.2\) GeV is needed to avoid correcting the data by a factor 10 or more. In analysis of the central state multiplicities greater then two, the same efficiency is used, but the two highest transverse momenta among the ID tracks are used.

