#### Limited \(|\Delta z_{0}|\) of the ID tracks (part of cut AC2.2)

Some small fraction of the CEP events was rejected with the cut \(|\Delta z_{0}|<20\) mm. Correction for the introduced inefficiency was calculated from the data as a function of the lower \(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) of two outermost tracks (those which determine the \(|\Delta z_{0}|\)) - the lower the \(p_{\mathrm{T}}\) is, the worse is the pointing resolution and thus the efficiency of the discussed cut drops. The efficiency was calculated as a ratio of the number of CEP events (after full selection and background subtraction) satisfying a limit \(|\Delta z_{0}|<20\) mm (denoted \(N_{B}\)) to number of CEP events without limited \(|\Delta z_{0}|\) (denoted \(N_{A}\)):

\[\varepsilon_{|\Delta z_{0}|}(\mathrm{min}(p_{\mathrm{T}}))=\frac{N_{B}( \mathrm{min}(p_{\mathrm{T}}))}{N_{A}(\mathrm{min}(p_{\mathrm{T}}))}. \tag{18.13}\]

