Figure 20.18 shows the differential cross sections for CEP of \(p\bar{p}\) pairs as a function of the pair invariant mass separately in two \(\Delta\varphi\) regions: \(\Delta\varphi<90^{\circ}\) and \(\Delta\varphi>90^{\circ}\). The data do not show a significant \(\Delta\varphi\) asymmetry except for a possible enhancement in the \(2.2-2.4\) GeV mass range for the \(\Delta\varphi>90^{\circ}\) region.

Angular distributions of the proton from the centrally-produced pair, calculated in the Collins-Soper reference frame, are shown in Fig. 20.19. In case of both \(d\sigma/d\cos\theta^{\text{CS}}\) and \(d\sigma/d\cos\phi^{\text{CS}}\) the statistical uncertainties make the comparisons of data with MC predictions difficult. The data demonstrate some asymmetries between positive and negative \(\cos\theta^{\text{CS}}\) and \(\phi^{\text{CS}}\), which are not supported by the MC predictions.

